 "meter": [
  "IN CLOSING \u00b7 WHAT IS SHOWN, AND WHAT IS NOT"
 ],
 "open": [
  false
 ],
 "note": [
  "THE CONCLUSION. Do not soften it and do not oversell it - the credibility of the whole talk is spent or kept here.\n\nTwo things are shown. A chain for one theorem that actually runs, and a structure whose load-bearing parts can be measured rather than guessed.\n\nThree things are not. The big extraction is not usable - every one of those six hundred nodes is blocked pending a review nobody has done. The chain that does run stands on a dependency graph I wrote by hand for this paper, and automatic library lookup - finding the matching declaration in Mathlib - is zero lines of code today. And none of this touches whether the formal object means the physics you had in mind; no kernel judges that.\n\nThen the last line, which is the honest version of the whole talk: the claim is not that this works. It is that it has become small enough to argue about. A year ago I could not have shown you a specific place where it stops."
 ],
